{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_softwood_cracked","model_identifier":"wall_softwood_cracked","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_softwood_cracked\n\nDamaged state below 70 % HP of `wall_softwood` (Patch 5): the same wooden (softwood) piece with dark cracks, a few tips or merlons knocked off and splinters or chips. The game swaps it in below 70 % HP and back above 70 % when repaired.\n\nSoftwood wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Timber (pale, rough, rope-lashed softwood logs), 3 m (106 u) with pointed tops and a fighting step behind at 78 u.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..110, z -7..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 14, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at x 0, z 2\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 78, 6)"},"resolution":{"width":128,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"log_wall_log0#9a7a50","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-8,0,-6],"to":[-4,106,-2],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0,0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[16,0,20,106],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[20,0,24,106],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[24,0,28,106],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[28,0,32,106],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[96,108,100,112],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[100,108,104,112